1
00:00:32,365 --> 00:00:39,372
‎FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

2
00:01:12,906 --> 00:01:13,823
‎Grandfather.

3
00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:18,244
‎Why?

4
00:01:19,871 --> 00:01:21,623
‎Why do you hate me so much?

5
00:01:22,248 --> 00:01:24,209
‎Because you have no talent.

6
00:01:24,292 --> 00:01:26,211
‎It's time to give up.

7
00:01:27,087 --> 00:01:29,380
‎You'll never make it.

8
00:01:29,964 --> 00:01:30,799
‎Grandfather…

9
00:01:33,843 --> 00:01:37,222
‎But I love music too.

10
00:01:40,725 --> 00:01:43,853
‎I love it so much.

11
00:01:45,104 --> 00:01:46,022
‎So why do you say…

12
00:01:48,399 --> 00:01:49,734
‎I'll never make it?

13
00:01:58,368 --> 00:01:59,494
‎Why not me?

14
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:03,081
‎Why?

15
00:02:06,584 --> 00:02:10,547
‎FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

16
00:02:16,052 --> 00:02:17,095
‎Why not me…

17
00:02:17,178 --> 00:02:18,888
‎EPISODE 5

18
00:02:19,973 --> 00:02:20,890
‎Why?

19
00:02:21,808 --> 00:02:22,892
‎-Why?
‎-Pi-o.

20
00:02:25,812 --> 00:02:27,021
‎Pi-o, what's wrong?

21
00:02:28,439 --> 00:02:29,732
‎Did you have another nightmare?

22
00:02:30,275 --> 00:02:31,234
‎No.

23
00:02:32,902 --> 00:02:33,903
‎Tell me.

24
00:02:35,071 --> 00:02:37,866
‎What nightmare wakes you up
‎every 30 minutes?

25
00:02:40,827 --> 00:02:41,995
‎Don't worry about it.

26
00:02:55,675 --> 00:02:59,762
‎CHOI JEONG-YO

27
00:03:17,405 --> 00:03:19,157
‎Why do you keep calling?

28
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:20,450
‎I'm sorry.

29
00:03:20,533 --> 00:03:21,784
‎I'm really sorry,

30
00:03:23,036 --> 00:03:26,748
‎but I'm outside the hospital
‎and would like to check in on Pi-o.

31
00:03:27,457 --> 00:03:29,083
‎How many times do I have to tell you?

32
00:03:29,876 --> 00:03:31,753
‎Pi-o doesn't want to see you.

33
00:03:32,503 --> 00:03:33,421
‎Don't you get it?

34
00:03:33,504 --> 00:03:34,505
‎But I…

35
00:03:48,102 --> 00:03:49,437
‎Why are you up?

36
00:03:51,314 --> 00:03:52,190
‎Get some more sleep.

37
00:03:58,279 --> 00:03:59,322
‎Was it Jeong-yo?

38
00:04:02,325 --> 00:04:03,159
‎No.

39
00:04:03,243 --> 00:04:04,786
‎Please call Jeong-yo for me.

40
00:04:06,537 --> 00:04:07,497
‎I need to talk to him.

41
00:04:08,373 --> 00:04:09,958
‎About what?

42
00:04:10,041 --> 00:04:11,501
‎Just wait until you're discharged.

43
00:04:11,584 --> 00:04:12,710
‎I said call him.

44
00:04:14,379 --> 00:04:15,213
‎Call Jeong-yo.

45
00:04:23,721 --> 00:04:24,722
‎KANG PI-O (MALE, 16 YEARS OLD)

46
00:04:29,644 --> 00:04:30,478
‎Thank you.

47
00:04:40,154 --> 00:04:41,489
‎Are you feeling better now?

48
00:04:42,448 --> 00:04:43,283
‎Yeah.

49
00:04:44,367 --> 00:04:45,243
‎Hey.

50
00:04:45,910 --> 00:04:48,955
‎Hospitalized for pneumonia?
‎What are you, a little kid?

51
00:04:49,038 --> 00:04:52,709
‎This is why I've been telling you
‎to eat and sleep well.

52
00:04:58,881 --> 00:05:00,008
‎When are you getting discharged?

53
00:05:00,967 --> 00:05:02,093
‎-Soon.
‎-Soon?

54
00:05:05,263 --> 00:05:07,140
‎Don't stay too long, okay?

55
00:05:07,223 --> 00:05:10,393
‎I'm bored out of my mind
‎because you're not around.

56
00:05:11,227 --> 00:05:13,771
‎Han-rim and Seok-hwan
‎are so full of themselves these days.

57
00:05:13,855 --> 00:05:15,565
‎They've been acting up,

58
00:05:15,648 --> 00:05:17,358
‎and it's driving me crazy.

59
00:05:18,526 --> 00:05:19,652
‎Jeez.

60
00:05:24,949 --> 00:05:26,617
‎I wanted to tell you something.

61
00:05:26,701 --> 00:05:27,827
‎You did?

62
00:05:29,412 --> 00:05:32,415
‎Go ahead. Tell me whatever it is.

63
00:05:37,420 --> 00:05:38,921
‎After I get discharged…

64
00:05:41,174 --> 00:05:42,925
‎I'm going to prepare
‎for the Harmonie Competition.

65
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:44,844
‎The competition?

66
00:05:44,927 --> 00:05:47,346
‎I thought you didn't want to
‎enter competitions anymore.

67
00:05:48,723 --> 00:05:50,808
‎How else can I prove myself if I don't?

68
00:05:51,392 --> 00:05:52,769
‎But still,

69
00:05:53,728 --> 00:05:55,772
‎I thought you wanted to
‎be happy making music.

70
00:05:56,314 --> 00:05:59,192
‎You said you were
‎tired of competing, so why?

71
00:05:59,275 --> 00:06:00,193
‎I'm not a genius.

72
00:06:01,652 --> 00:06:04,572
‎If I don't prove myself on stage,
‎who will listen to me play?

73
00:06:06,824 --> 00:06:08,367
‎The reason I called you here

74
00:06:09,702 --> 00:06:10,995
‎is to ask you…

75
00:06:12,747 --> 00:06:14,207
‎to enter the same competition.

76
00:06:14,749 --> 00:06:15,583
‎What?

77
00:06:16,167 --> 00:06:17,376
‎Don't say no.

78
00:06:18,795 --> 00:06:20,546
‎If I'm really your friend,

79
00:06:21,881 --> 00:06:23,633
‎you'll do me this favor.

80
00:06:24,675 --> 00:06:26,803
‎-But that's just--
‎-Why?

81
00:06:27,887 --> 00:06:29,972
‎Do you think you're guaranteed to win?

82
00:06:30,890 --> 00:06:33,935
‎You're wrong.
‎Things won't go your way this time.

83
00:06:34,727 --> 00:06:35,645
‎I already told you.

84
00:06:36,854 --> 00:06:39,440
‎I'll do whatever it takes to prove myself.

85
00:06:40,399 --> 00:06:42,068
‎But don't you dare lose on purpose.

86
00:06:43,319 --> 00:06:45,154
‎If I catch wind of that…

87
00:06:47,573 --> 00:06:49,075
‎I'm going to kill you.

88
00:06:53,913 --> 00:06:54,789
‎Fine.

89
00:06:58,334 --> 00:07:01,254
‎But you'd better practice really hard,

90
00:07:01,337 --> 00:07:03,422
‎or I'll wipe the floor with you.

91
00:07:05,383 --> 00:07:07,009
‎By the way, you can't kill me.

92
00:07:17,979 --> 00:07:19,063
‎You made the right call.

93
00:07:20,481 --> 00:07:22,191
‎Like you said, placing in competitions

94
00:07:23,317 --> 00:07:25,403
‎is the only way to play professionally.

95
00:07:25,486 --> 00:07:27,655
‎-Let's prepare well and--
‎-Don't get excited.

96
00:07:28,739 --> 00:07:30,199
‎If I don't win the competition…

97
00:07:33,744 --> 00:07:35,121
‎I'm going to quit the piano.

98
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:37,540
‎I'd rather quit…

99
00:07:40,418 --> 00:07:41,461
‎than be a mediocre pianist.

100
00:07:46,966 --> 00:07:48,092
‎Do you want to

101
00:07:48,759 --> 00:07:50,178
‎enter the competition?

102
00:07:52,805 --> 00:07:53,639
‎No.

103
00:07:54,223 --> 00:07:55,308
‎Then why are you doing it?

104
00:07:56,434 --> 00:07:57,685
‎I have to enter…

105
00:08:00,771 --> 00:08:03,441
‎to help Pi-o get back on his feet.

106
00:08:07,653 --> 00:08:09,906
‎If he needs me to light a fire under him,

107
00:08:11,532 --> 00:08:13,409
‎I'll gladly do it.

108
00:08:16,662 --> 00:08:17,538
‎All right.

109
00:08:18,873 --> 00:08:20,291
‎Let's do it.

110
00:08:20,374 --> 00:08:21,209
‎Okay.

111
00:08:21,292 --> 00:08:23,586
‎But I need you to promise me something.

112
00:08:24,212 --> 00:08:26,130
‎If you're just going to
‎play a supporting role,

113
00:08:27,465 --> 00:08:28,466
‎stop right now.

114
00:08:30,051 --> 00:08:31,844
‎I care for you and Pi-o

115
00:08:32,553 --> 00:08:34,555
‎equally as my students.

116
00:08:37,725 --> 00:08:39,936
‎If I catch you not giving it your all,

117
00:08:41,521 --> 00:08:43,523
‎I won't let it slide.

118
00:08:48,903 --> 00:08:50,488
‎Why is he wearing headphones during lunch?

119
00:08:50,571 --> 00:08:51,739
‎Seriously.

120
00:09:48,337 --> 00:09:49,755
‎Congratulations.

121
00:10:29,420 --> 00:10:31,005
‎Good afternoon, contestants.

122
00:10:31,088 --> 00:10:34,091
‎Congratulations on advancing
‎to the main round

123
00:10:34,175 --> 00:10:37,261
‎of the Prague Harmonie
‎International Competition.

124
00:10:40,181 --> 00:10:43,643
‎First, allow me to outline
‎the competition schedule.

125
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:47,438
‎This week, 24 contestants

126
00:10:47,521 --> 00:10:51,525
‎will be selected from
‎approximately 60 main round participants

127
00:10:52,026 --> 00:10:54,153
‎to advance to the semifinals.

128
00:10:54,236 --> 00:10:58,532
‎Those 24 semifinalists
‎will be competing next week.

129
00:10:59,367 --> 00:11:02,370
‎From there, 12 finalists will be chosen,

130
00:11:02,453 --> 00:11:05,539
‎and they will move
‎from their homestays to the chapel

131
00:11:06,457 --> 00:11:09,168
‎where all mobile phones
‎and electronic devices

132
00:11:09,251 --> 00:11:10,753
‎will be confiscated.

133
00:11:11,629 --> 00:11:14,298
‎And they will reside together
‎for one week.

134
00:11:14,382 --> 00:11:17,843
‎SEMIFINALS
‎QUALIFYING ROUND FOR THE TOP 24

135
00:11:18,552 --> 00:11:20,805
‎Contestant number 15,

136
00:11:20,888 --> 00:11:24,016
‎Jeong-yo Choi, please come to the stage.

137
00:12:15,734 --> 00:12:17,069
‎You've got to be kidding me.

138
00:12:18,028 --> 00:12:19,071
‎Where'd this guy come from?

139
00:12:19,155 --> 00:12:22,241
‎I have no idea, but damn it,
‎he's ridiculously good.

140
00:12:51,896 --> 00:12:52,855
‎Fine.

141
00:12:53,439 --> 00:12:54,648
‎His technique, yeah.

142
00:12:55,566 --> 00:12:58,194
‎Genuinely… untouchable.

143
00:12:59,487 --> 00:13:00,988
‎No one even comes close to that.

144
00:13:24,011 --> 00:13:25,638
‎What's wrong with your pinky finger?

145
00:13:30,518 --> 00:13:32,561
‎If you keep playing, you'll destroy it.

146
00:13:33,521 --> 00:13:35,606
‎Give practice a rest
‎and get it treated first.

147
00:13:37,191 --> 00:13:39,318
‎I don't know what you saw,
‎but stop being dramatic.

148
00:13:39,401 --> 00:13:41,320
‎Mind your own business
‎and worry about yourself.

149
00:14:01,423 --> 00:14:02,466
‎You're okay, right?

150
00:14:03,551 --> 00:14:04,760
‎Are you taking

151
00:14:05,636 --> 00:14:06,929
‎your medication?

152
00:14:08,055 --> 00:14:08,889
‎Yes.

153
00:14:09,473 --> 00:14:10,432
‎Good.

154
00:14:11,350 --> 00:14:13,561
‎Hang in there for three more weeks.

155
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:17,648
‎I'll get stronger meds from the hospital,
‎so just bear with it.

156
00:14:17,731 --> 00:14:19,149
‎We've worked too hard to get here.

157
00:14:20,150 --> 00:14:21,277
‎It'd be such a shame

158
00:14:22,528 --> 00:14:25,197
‎to give up now after all this, right?

159
00:15:25,841 --> 00:15:26,884
‎Where have you been?

160
00:15:29,470 --> 00:15:31,013
‎Why aren't you in bed?

161
00:15:32,514 --> 00:15:33,807
‎Have you been practicing until now?

162
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:36,685
‎What if you wear yourself out?

163
00:15:37,269 --> 00:15:39,897
‎Is it unusual to practice until 4 a.m.?

164
00:15:40,481 --> 00:15:44,234
‎Or is it unusual to be out
‎until this hour?

165
00:15:46,070 --> 00:15:49,281
‎I went for a drive because I'm jet-lagged.

166
00:15:49,365 --> 00:15:50,658
‎Go to bed.

167
00:15:50,741 --> 00:15:53,994
‎It'll only get tougher starting tomorrow,
‎so you need to pace yourself.

168
00:16:00,793 --> 00:16:04,880
‎TOP 12 FINALIST ANNOUNCEMENT

169
00:16:05,381 --> 00:16:07,174
‎The first finalist is

170
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:08,926
‎Pi-o Kang.

171
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:24,858
‎The second finalist is

172
00:16:25,693 --> 00:16:26,860
‎Jeong-yo Choi.

173
00:16:37,496 --> 00:16:39,123
‎The third finalist is

174
00:16:39,873 --> 00:16:41,083
‎Tom Harrison.

175
00:17:07,693 --> 00:17:09,111
‎Welcome to the chapel.

176
00:17:09,194 --> 00:17:13,032
‎From this point on,
‎no outsiders are permitted.

177
00:17:13,115 --> 00:17:16,035
‎You may say your goodbyes
‎to your mother here.

178
00:17:17,369 --> 00:17:19,580
‎You'll do great, right?

179
00:17:21,290 --> 00:17:22,124
‎Yes.

180
00:17:31,383 --> 00:17:32,760
‎As you already know,

181
00:17:32,843 --> 00:17:36,096
‎I'm sure you chose a free piece
‎you're confident in,

182
00:17:36,180 --> 00:17:39,767
‎but the assigned piece is
‎far more difficult than you can imagine.

183
00:17:40,642 --> 00:17:45,397
‎Since it's a contemporary piece,
‎interpreting it won't be easy either.

184
00:17:45,981 --> 00:17:46,857
‎So…

185
00:17:48,859 --> 00:17:51,528
‎You must not lose
‎the set piece sheet music

186
00:17:51,612 --> 00:17:53,697
‎under any circumstances.

187
00:17:53,781 --> 00:17:56,575
‎If it's lost due to your own negligence,

188
00:17:56,658 --> 00:17:58,160
‎it will not be reissued.

189
00:18:04,416 --> 00:18:06,418
‎Now, your phone please.

190
00:18:09,797 --> 00:18:10,672
‎Here it is.

191
00:18:11,507 --> 00:18:12,549
‎Good luck.

192
00:18:12,633 --> 00:18:13,842
‎Thank you.

193
00:19:07,563 --> 00:19:08,897
‎As of today,

194
00:19:08,981 --> 00:19:12,276
‎all 12 finalists
‎officially moved into the chapel.

195
00:19:13,402 --> 00:19:17,072
‎Tomorrow, reporters from around the world
‎will be arriving.

196
00:19:17,573 --> 00:19:20,951
‎After that, performances
‎will take place in order,

197
00:19:21,451 --> 00:19:23,162
‎two contestants at a time.

198
00:19:24,163 --> 00:19:29,877
‎This will be the first
‎and last banquet with everyone,

199
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:32,921
‎so please enjoy the meal.

200
00:19:44,183 --> 00:19:45,517
‎How's your pinky finger?

201
00:19:47,227 --> 00:19:48,812
‎I said mind your own business.

202
00:19:48,896 --> 00:19:51,190
‎This is the last time
‎I'm asking, you punk.

203
00:19:53,192 --> 00:19:56,069
‎We don't even have time to eat right now,
‎and they're talking about a banquet?

204
00:19:56,904 --> 00:19:59,281
‎Honestly, I'd much rather just have
‎one more day to practice.

205
00:19:59,364 --> 00:20:03,327
‎Like, how exactly are we supposed to
‎master two pieces in seven days?

206
00:20:03,410 --> 00:20:04,620
‎That's crazy, right?

207
00:20:04,703 --> 00:20:06,288
‎I mean, that's exactly what I'm saying.

208
00:20:06,997 --> 00:20:09,958
‎Like, the pressure is so intense,
‎I can't even sleep.

209
00:20:11,001 --> 00:20:12,878
‎How is everyone doing with the set piece?

210
00:20:12,961 --> 00:20:15,923
‎Isn't this the hardest song
‎we have ever gotten?

211
00:20:16,006 --> 00:20:18,675
‎I have been analyzing the score for days,

212
00:20:18,759 --> 00:20:20,093
‎and I still have no clue.

213
00:20:21,887 --> 00:20:23,972
‎Hey, how about you guys?

214
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:25,891
‎How's the set piece for you?

215
00:20:25,974 --> 00:20:26,975
‎Pretty easy?

216
00:20:27,726 --> 00:20:29,019
‎Must have been easy.

217
00:20:29,102 --> 00:20:31,980
‎There's apparently no such thing
‎as a difficult piece for the Koreans.

218
00:20:33,106 --> 00:20:34,566
‎Absolute practice addicts.

219
00:20:36,485 --> 00:20:39,112
‎Hey, what did she just say?

220
00:20:39,196 --> 00:20:40,322
‎Was she talking trash?

221
00:20:40,405 --> 00:20:42,407
‎She's asking if we find the set piece
‎easy or hard.

222
00:20:45,702 --> 00:20:46,912
‎Difficult, difficult.

223
00:20:48,038 --> 00:20:49,206
‎Hard, hard.

224
00:20:49,790 --> 00:20:52,584
‎But hard training, good.

225
00:20:53,085 --> 00:20:54,586
‎Then what did you pick
‎for your free piece?

226
00:20:54,670 --> 00:20:55,837
‎"Beep beep?"

227
00:20:55,921 --> 00:20:57,422
‎Free piece.

228
00:21:01,426 --> 00:21:02,761
‎She's asking what piece you prepared.

229
00:21:06,014 --> 00:21:08,892
‎Rachmaninoff's Concerto No. 2.

230
00:21:18,902 --> 00:21:19,903
‎The second concerto?

231
00:21:21,947 --> 00:21:23,824
‎I want to play the third one.

232
00:21:24,449 --> 00:21:25,617
‎No.

233
00:21:25,701 --> 00:21:26,994
‎In my opinion,

234
00:21:27,619 --> 00:21:30,956
‎the piece that will help you
‎grow more in the long run

235
00:21:31,039 --> 00:21:32,666
‎is the second one.

236
00:21:33,250 --> 00:21:34,626
‎But I find the third one

237
00:21:35,794 --> 00:21:38,255
‎-easier than the second.
‎-Pi-o.

238
00:21:38,338 --> 00:21:40,674
‎Technique shouldn't be your main goal.

239
00:21:40,757 --> 00:21:43,719
‎You need to choose a piece
‎based on musicality and emotion.

240
00:21:44,344 --> 00:21:46,221
‎You need to push past your limits

241
00:21:47,139 --> 00:21:48,640
‎to win in the end.

242
00:21:50,684 --> 00:21:51,560
‎Pi-o.

243
00:21:53,186 --> 00:21:54,146
‎Have faith in yourself.

244
00:21:56,648 --> 00:21:58,734
‎Why did he have us play the same piece?

245
00:22:49,451 --> 00:22:51,119
‎Do you have any idea what time it is?

246
00:22:51,203 --> 00:22:52,204
‎Why should I?

247
00:22:52,287 --> 00:22:53,538
‎How am I supposed to sleep

248
00:22:53,622 --> 00:22:56,416
‎when all I can hear
‎is the sound of that damn piano?

249
00:22:56,500 --> 00:22:57,918
‎Take it to the administration.

250
00:22:58,001 --> 00:23:01,088
‎It's not my fault
‎the rooms aren't soundproof!

251
00:23:01,588 --> 00:23:02,589
‎Hey, hey!

252
00:23:03,632 --> 00:23:05,383
‎Open the damn door!

253
00:23:05,467 --> 00:23:06,384
‎Pi-o!

254
00:23:07,594 --> 00:23:10,639
‎You bastard, open the door!
‎I said right now!

255
00:23:11,473 --> 00:23:12,891
‎Open the door!

256
00:23:13,642 --> 00:23:16,937
‎No easy. Little bit difficult.

257
00:23:17,020 --> 00:23:18,897
‎-Just a little bit? Okay.
‎-Yes, a little bit.

258
00:23:19,481 --> 00:23:20,315
‎And…

259
00:23:20,398 --> 00:23:21,691
‎So despite your young age,

260
00:23:21,775 --> 00:23:24,111
‎you've amazed the world
‎with flawless technique.

261
00:23:24,194 --> 00:23:25,654
‎How did you start to play the piano?

262
00:23:27,823 --> 00:23:30,117
‎I was told that my family noticed me

263
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:34,162
‎play songs from TV
‎when I was around three years old.

264
00:23:34,246 --> 00:23:35,372
‎Three years old?

265
00:23:36,206 --> 00:23:37,499
‎So you are a genius.

266
00:23:38,500 --> 00:23:41,962
‎I heard that you're the grandson
‎of Maestro Seung-woon Kang.

267
00:23:42,045 --> 00:23:46,049
‎His fans are eagerly wondering
‎whether we might see a collaboration

268
00:23:46,133 --> 00:23:48,885
‎-between a grandfather as a conductor
‎-Music made me powerful…

269
00:23:48,969 --> 00:23:51,138
‎and his grandson as a pianist.

270
00:23:51,221 --> 00:23:52,264
‎Did you hear that?

271
00:23:54,516 --> 00:23:55,517
‎I'd like that.

272
00:24:20,834 --> 00:24:21,710
‎Go ahead.

273
00:24:24,004 --> 00:24:25,547
‎Start from the coda
‎of the second movement.

274
00:24:25,630 --> 00:24:29,801
‎CODA: ITALIAN FOR "TAIL,"
‎THE MEMORABLE CLOSING SECTION OF A PIECE

275
00:25:23,396 --> 00:25:24,481
‎Stop.

276
00:25:31,363 --> 00:25:32,447
‎You'd be better off…

277
00:25:34,908 --> 00:25:37,535
‎asking Baryshnikov to do it instead of me.

278
00:25:40,372 --> 00:25:41,665
‎Why?

279
00:25:42,374 --> 00:25:45,168
‎Because he'd be a better fit
‎for your performance.

280
00:25:48,755 --> 00:25:50,298
‎Please tell me why.

281
00:25:51,633 --> 00:25:53,093
‎You'd conduct for anyone else.

282
00:25:53,176 --> 00:25:55,553
‎No, I know you'll conduct for Jeong-yo.

283
00:25:56,429 --> 00:25:58,139
‎But why are you refusing me?

284
00:26:01,351 --> 00:26:02,811
‎I just told you.

285
00:26:04,020 --> 00:26:06,773
‎He'd be a better fit for your performance.

286
00:26:06,856 --> 00:26:09,776
‎We're both conductors for the competition,
‎so what's the problem?

287
00:26:37,762 --> 00:26:38,596
‎What are you doing?

288
00:26:40,223 --> 00:26:41,599
‎Why are you lurking like that?

289
00:27:03,246 --> 00:27:04,289
‎Pi-o.

290
00:27:04,372 --> 00:27:06,166
‎Technique shouldn't be your main goal.

291
00:27:06,249 --> 00:27:09,210
‎You need to choose a piece
‎based on musicality and emotion.

292
00:27:18,636 --> 00:27:20,221
‎You'd be better off…

293
00:27:20,305 --> 00:27:23,475
‎asking Baryshnikov to do it
‎instead of me.

294
00:27:23,558 --> 00:27:25,101
‎I just told you.

295
00:27:25,185 --> 00:27:27,312
‎He'd be a better fit for your performance.

296
00:27:28,146 --> 00:27:28,980
‎Pi-o Kang!

297
00:27:29,564 --> 00:27:31,274
‎Enough is enough!

298
00:27:31,358 --> 00:27:33,109
‎How many days has it been, huh?

299
00:27:33,193 --> 00:27:34,986
‎You trying to ruin my competition?

300
00:27:36,363 --> 00:27:37,572
‎If you can't stand it,

301
00:27:37,655 --> 00:27:39,240
‎ask them to switch your room.

302
00:27:39,324 --> 00:27:40,575
‎Why do you keep harassing me?

303
00:27:40,658 --> 00:27:42,619
‎No, no, I told you to switch

304
00:27:42,702 --> 00:27:44,954
‎because the piano in that room
‎suits me best.

305
00:27:45,038 --> 00:27:46,414
‎Don't be stupid.

306
00:27:46,498 --> 00:27:48,249
‎Why would I waste my time like that?

307
00:27:50,585 --> 00:27:52,295
‎You selfish bastard.

308
00:27:52,379 --> 00:27:54,589
‎Spying on people, huh? Like a rat!

309
00:27:56,508 --> 00:27:58,134
‎Hey, knock it off!

310
00:27:58,718 --> 00:28:00,678
‎Stop, stop!

311
00:28:00,762 --> 00:28:01,721
‎Cut it out.

312
00:28:01,805 --> 00:28:04,182
‎Do you want to get kicked out
‎before you even compete?

313
00:28:04,682 --> 00:28:07,310
‎He's just defending you because
‎you guys are from the same country.

314
00:28:07,394 --> 00:28:08,520
‎It's pathetic.

315
00:28:08,603 --> 00:28:11,272
‎Does he even know that you've been
‎eavesdropping on his performance?

316
00:28:11,356 --> 00:28:12,190
‎Shut up!

317
00:28:12,273 --> 00:28:14,150
‎Hey, I said knock it off!

318
00:28:14,234 --> 00:28:15,318
‎You crazy bastard.

319
00:28:15,402 --> 00:28:16,611
‎Out, now!

320
00:28:17,195 --> 00:28:18,405
‎What a psychopath!

321
00:28:18,988 --> 00:28:20,198
‎Come on!

322
00:28:25,495 --> 00:28:27,080
‎You need to eat as you practice

323
00:28:27,163 --> 00:28:29,916
‎so you can actually fight back
‎at times like this.

324
00:28:33,586 --> 00:28:35,088
‎You're not yourself right now.

325
00:28:35,171 --> 00:28:37,382
‎Stop stressing and get a hold of yourself.

326
00:28:37,924 --> 00:28:40,760
‎Go take a walk and get some good sleep.

327
00:28:41,469 --> 00:28:44,347
‎Practicing all night won't help.

328
00:28:44,431 --> 00:28:47,308
‎Guys like you can afford that luxury.

329
00:28:47,892 --> 00:28:50,937
‎You know practice is everything
‎to people like me.

330
00:28:51,730 --> 00:28:52,856
‎Get out of my way.

331
00:28:52,939 --> 00:28:54,941
‎Come on, Pi-o!

332
00:28:55,024 --> 00:28:57,026
‎I said get out of my way!

333
00:29:47,076 --> 00:29:48,077
‎Open the door.

334
00:29:49,329 --> 00:29:50,663
‎Open the door!

335
00:29:53,208 --> 00:29:54,542
‎What is it now? Hey!

336
00:29:55,543 --> 00:29:56,795
‎What are you doing?

337
00:29:57,378 --> 00:29:58,546
‎This is my room. Get out!

338
00:30:00,757 --> 00:30:02,258
‎What are you doing?

339
00:30:04,677 --> 00:30:05,678
‎What are you doing?

340
00:30:06,554 --> 00:30:08,181
‎Where'd you hide my sheet music?

341
00:30:08,264 --> 00:30:09,557
‎What the hell are you talking about?

342
00:30:10,475 --> 00:30:13,770
‎You stole it to screw me over
‎while I was gone.

343
00:30:13,853 --> 00:30:15,271
‎Why on earth are you in here?

344
00:30:15,355 --> 00:30:16,731
‎Use your words!

345
00:30:16,815 --> 00:30:18,191
‎You're insane.

346
00:30:18,274 --> 00:30:19,943
‎Where's my sheet music?

347
00:30:24,280 --> 00:30:26,407
‎Pi-o. Kang Pi-o!

348
00:30:26,491 --> 00:30:27,867
‎He's lost it.

349
00:30:27,951 --> 00:30:30,161
‎Pi-o, you're completely insane!

350
00:30:40,922 --> 00:30:41,840
‎Pi-o.

351
00:30:45,385 --> 00:30:46,344
‎Kang Pi-o!

352
00:30:54,102 --> 00:30:55,061
‎No.

353
00:30:59,524 --> 00:31:00,525
‎Kang Pi-o!

354
00:31:03,778 --> 00:31:05,154
‎Hey, stop!

355
00:31:05,238 --> 00:31:06,197
‎Let go of me!

356
00:31:06,990 --> 00:31:08,074
‎Come on, get out!

357
00:31:08,575 --> 00:31:09,742
‎I said let go!

358
00:31:14,038 --> 00:31:15,290
‎Come on.

359
00:31:15,373 --> 00:31:16,541
‎Get out!

360
00:31:17,917 --> 00:31:18,751
‎Enough!

361
00:31:27,176 --> 00:31:28,595
‎Are you insane?

362
00:31:28,678 --> 00:31:29,762
‎This is all your fault.

363
00:31:30,388 --> 00:31:32,015
‎It's all your fault!

364
00:31:42,191 --> 00:31:43,568
‎It's just the piano.

365
00:31:44,527 --> 00:31:46,279
‎Why tear yourself apart over music?

366
00:31:47,447 --> 00:31:49,198
‎You're way more important
‎than any of that.

367
00:31:49,782 --> 00:31:52,201
‎So why the hell
‎are you doing this to yourself?

368
00:32:06,591 --> 00:32:08,676
‎Has this Pi-o Kang guy
‎just completely gone mad?

369
00:32:08,760 --> 00:32:12,055
‎If you can't handle the pressure,
‎you shouldn't be competing at all.

370
00:32:12,639 --> 00:32:15,558
‎Seriously, how can one person
‎cause this much trouble for everyone else?

371
00:32:16,976 --> 00:32:19,145
‎All right, let's head in.

372
00:32:19,228 --> 00:32:21,522
‎Anna, you should
‎get some rest for tomorrow.

373
00:32:22,357 --> 00:32:23,191
‎You're right.

374
00:32:25,443 --> 00:32:26,277
‎Wait.

375
00:32:27,737 --> 00:32:28,696
‎Is that…

376
00:32:29,948 --> 00:32:31,074
‎really true?

377
00:32:32,659 --> 00:32:36,371
‎You are not lying to me, are you?

378
00:32:37,789 --> 00:32:38,748
‎What?

379
00:32:39,791 --> 00:32:41,292
‎Are you saying one of us did it?

380
00:32:44,671 --> 00:32:45,838
‎Sorry.

381
00:32:49,801 --> 00:32:50,635
‎Look.

382
00:32:51,135 --> 00:32:53,930
‎No one went out into the garden. See?

383
00:32:54,013 --> 00:32:56,182
‎Isn't there a CCTV in the hallway?

384
00:32:56,849 --> 00:32:59,477
‎That area is for staff only,
‎so there are no cameras.

385
00:32:59,560 --> 00:33:00,478
‎Pi-o.

386
00:33:01,104 --> 00:33:04,357
‎Maybe you should try to think carefully
‎about where you might have left it.

387
00:33:05,149 --> 00:33:06,818
‎If it turns up somewhere else later,

388
00:33:07,568 --> 00:33:08,945
‎this could end badly for you.

389
00:33:10,029 --> 00:33:13,408
‎Are you sure this isn't a panic attack
‎from too much pressure?

390
00:33:13,491 --> 00:33:15,034
‎Maybe you should withdraw

391
00:33:15,118 --> 00:33:16,244
‎and go see a doctor.

392
00:33:33,052 --> 00:33:35,013
‎DAY 4 OF THE FINAL ROUND

393
00:33:35,096 --> 00:33:36,848
‎-Bye, guys.
‎-Good luck.

394
00:33:36,931 --> 00:33:38,141
‎You got this.

395
00:33:39,100 --> 00:33:40,560
‎-Thanks.
‎-You can do it.

396
00:34:00,955 --> 00:34:02,749
‎KANG PI-O

397
00:34:02,832 --> 00:34:04,083
‎-Let go of me!
‎-Out, now!

398
00:34:05,043 --> 00:34:06,502
‎What a psychopath!

399
00:34:06,586 --> 00:34:07,920
‎You know what? Try that again,

400
00:34:08,004 --> 00:34:09,464
‎and I'll smash your face.

401
00:35:08,898 --> 00:35:11,150
‎Turn it off. It's too bright.

402
00:35:11,234 --> 00:35:14,445
‎Get up and eat some of this
‎before you get sick.

403
00:35:23,246 --> 00:35:26,082
‎How long are you going to lie around?
‎What about practice?

404
00:35:28,126 --> 00:35:29,168
‎Get out.

405
00:35:33,673 --> 00:35:36,467
‎You shouldn't be lounging around.

406
00:35:37,552 --> 00:35:40,012
‎I said I'd wipe the floor with you
‎if you didn't practice hard.

407
00:35:47,520 --> 00:35:48,646
‎I'm going to withdraw.

408
00:35:57,029 --> 00:35:57,864
‎What?

409
00:35:58,447 --> 00:35:59,323
‎Hey.

410
00:36:00,241 --> 00:36:02,076
‎What kind of nonsense is that?

411
00:36:03,077 --> 00:36:05,329
‎Why would you withdraw
‎over some sheet music?

412
00:36:06,372 --> 00:36:08,332
‎Have you really lost your mind?

413
00:36:08,958 --> 00:36:09,876
‎Yeah.

414
00:36:12,503 --> 00:36:13,880
‎Maybe I have.

415
00:36:14,714 --> 00:36:15,923
‎I don't know if I hallucinated

416
00:36:17,383 --> 00:36:19,385
‎or if I was out of my mind.

417
00:36:22,555 --> 00:36:23,931
‎I don't know if I lost it

418
00:36:25,558 --> 00:36:27,059
‎or if it was stolen.

419
00:36:28,728 --> 00:36:30,146
‎Still,

420
00:36:30,229 --> 00:36:32,773
‎there's no way
‎you haven't memorized it already.

421
00:36:35,234 --> 00:36:36,736
‎Losing it doesn't mean--

422
00:36:36,819 --> 00:36:38,279
‎Memorizing it isn't the issue.

423
00:36:39,780 --> 00:36:41,324
‎I couldn't interpret it.

424
00:36:42,450 --> 00:36:45,411
‎And that scared me.

425
00:36:46,871 --> 00:36:48,122
‎Even if I compete…

426
00:36:51,667 --> 00:36:52,960
‎I'll just get eliminated.

427
00:36:55,546 --> 00:36:56,797
‎I know it.

428
00:36:58,382 --> 00:36:59,926
‎This is probably for the best.

429
00:37:01,344 --> 00:37:02,303
‎The truth is…

430
00:37:04,597 --> 00:37:05,765
‎I already knew.

431
00:37:06,891 --> 00:37:08,434
‎I knew entering this competition

432
00:37:09,477 --> 00:37:11,395
‎was too ambitious of me.

433
00:37:15,233 --> 00:37:17,693
‎And I knew becoming a great pianist

434
00:37:18,778 --> 00:37:22,156
‎was too big a dream for me.

435
00:37:24,116 --> 00:37:25,076
‎But…

436
00:37:26,911 --> 00:37:28,496
‎I loved the piano too much…

437
00:37:30,831 --> 00:37:32,375
‎to give it up.

438
00:37:34,418 --> 00:37:37,672
‎I loved music too much.

439
00:37:38,881 --> 00:37:39,799
‎That's why

440
00:37:41,092 --> 00:37:42,510
‎I did whatever I could

441
00:37:43,719 --> 00:37:45,846
‎to play those beautiful songs‎…

442
00:37:47,765 --> 00:37:49,100
‎with my own hands.

443
00:37:49,725 --> 00:37:51,644
‎I knew I was being too ambitious,

444
00:37:52,979 --> 00:37:54,146
‎but I couldn't give up.

445
00:38:01,737 --> 00:38:02,989
‎I'm walking away now…

446
00:38:05,032 --> 00:38:06,367
‎from this unrequited love.

447
00:38:10,496 --> 00:38:13,833
‎I feel like I've done all that I can.

448
00:38:17,253 --> 00:38:18,170
‎And…

449
00:38:19,922 --> 00:38:21,674
‎I owe you an apology.

450
00:38:24,218 --> 00:38:26,262
‎I projected my inferiority and self-doubt

451
00:38:26,971 --> 00:38:30,182
‎onto you for no reason.

452
00:38:30,850 --> 00:38:32,435
‎I'm going to quit now…

453
00:38:34,937 --> 00:38:36,939
‎but I hope you'll keep going.

454
00:38:41,152 --> 00:38:42,194
‎Please leave.

455
00:38:43,446 --> 00:38:44,447
‎I want to sleep.

456
00:39:18,564 --> 00:39:20,358
‎This is all your fault.

457
00:39:20,441 --> 00:39:21,776
‎It's all your fault!

458
00:39:24,195 --> 00:39:25,654
‎I owe you an apology.

459
00:39:27,323 --> 00:39:29,283
‎I projected my inferiority and self-doubt

460
00:39:30,534 --> 00:39:32,203
‎onto you for no reason.

461
00:39:36,832 --> 00:39:39,126
‎But I need you to promise me something.

462
00:39:39,710 --> 00:39:41,670
‎If you're just going to
‎play a supporting role,

463
00:39:43,047 --> 00:39:44,131
‎stop right now.

464
00:41:36,577 --> 00:41:38,996
‎CHOI JEONG-YO

465
00:42:23,541 --> 00:42:24,625
‎I've memorized everything.

466
00:42:25,459 --> 00:42:26,710
‎Take it if you need it.

467
00:42:38,847 --> 00:42:40,140
‎IN SYNC WITH THE WIND INSTRUMENTS

468
00:42:40,224 --> 00:42:41,225
‎LISTEN TO THE RHYTHM

469
00:42:43,686 --> 00:42:45,563
‎ADD ANOTHER TIMBRE,
‎LIKE I'M HOLDING MY BREATH

470
00:42:45,646 --> 00:42:46,981
‎EASY ON THE CRESCENDO

471
00:43:37,656 --> 00:43:41,577
‎LAST DAY OF THE FINAL ROUND

472
00:44:18,155 --> 00:44:19,156
‎Good luck.

473
00:44:20,824 --> 00:44:21,700
‎Thank you.

474
00:44:48,686 --> 00:44:53,357
‎We are at the Prague Harmonie
‎International Competition finals venue.

475
00:44:53,440 --> 00:44:56,860
‎Today is the final round,
‎featuring the two finalists.

476
00:44:56,944 --> 00:45:00,864
‎Following their exceptional
‎semifinal performances,

477
00:45:00,948 --> 00:45:04,076
‎all attention is focused
‎on today's event.

478
00:45:10,040 --> 00:45:12,084
‎The assigned piece is a nightmare,

479
00:45:12,167 --> 00:45:14,044
‎so there's no telling
‎how this will play out.

480
00:45:14,628 --> 00:45:16,713
‎Don't worry. Jeong-yo will do great.

481
00:45:41,697 --> 00:45:42,573
‎See you again.

482
00:45:43,323 --> 00:45:44,158
‎Thank you.

483
00:45:48,912 --> 00:45:51,832
‎You are the final performer
‎of the competition.

484
00:45:51,915 --> 00:45:55,252
‎We are all looking forward
‎to a wonderful performance.

485
00:45:56,378 --> 00:45:57,421
‎Okay. Thank you.

486
00:45:59,047 --> 00:46:00,716
‎-Bye.
‎-Bye.

487
00:46:03,552 --> 00:46:04,511
‎Thank you.

488
00:46:49,389 --> 00:46:51,058
‎What just happened?

489
00:46:51,850 --> 00:46:53,685
‎Is that really the Kang Pi-o I know?

490
00:47:26,301 --> 00:47:29,638
‎Mr. Kang. That was amazing, really.

491
00:47:29,721 --> 00:47:30,722
‎Thank you.

492
00:47:31,640 --> 00:47:33,892
‎Your performance is so unique.

493
00:47:33,976 --> 00:47:36,895
‎If you do just as well in the free piece,
‎you're bound to win.

494
00:47:52,452 --> 00:47:54,496
‎Did you check if the money came in?

495
00:47:54,580 --> 00:47:55,581
‎I did.

496
00:47:56,915 --> 00:47:58,792
‎Then where's my advance payment?

497
00:47:58,875 --> 00:48:00,544
‎Do I look like a pushover to you?

498
00:48:00,627 --> 00:48:02,879
‎I said you'd get paid after the job.

499
00:48:02,963 --> 00:48:04,381
‎What's with all the whining?

500
00:49:30,092 --> 00:49:31,760
‎Where are we going now?

501
00:49:33,220 --> 00:49:37,516
‎Isn't this the opposite direction
‎from the concert hall?

502
00:49:39,017 --> 00:49:40,185
‎Excuse me.

503
00:49:40,268 --> 00:49:41,520
‎Stop, stop!

504
00:49:41,603 --> 00:49:43,397
‎I want to go to the toilet!

505
00:49:44,856 --> 00:49:45,899
‎Are you listening to me?

506
00:49:45,982 --> 00:49:48,026
‎I said I need to go to the restroom!

507
00:49:49,361 --> 00:49:50,195
‎Cut the crap!

508
00:49:50,779 --> 00:49:52,948
‎Or else I'll put a bullet
‎through your head.

509
00:50:27,649 --> 00:50:30,610
‎Watch it before you drive us into a grave.

510
00:50:30,694 --> 00:50:31,611
‎No, you watch it.

511
00:50:31,695 --> 00:50:33,488
‎Don't get blood splatter in the car.

512
00:50:34,781 --> 00:50:38,660
‎Who do you think you are?
‎Don't tell me what to do.

513
00:50:38,744 --> 00:50:40,203
‎You want me to kill you first?

514
00:50:40,287 --> 00:50:42,581
‎Just focus on driving, you piece of crap!

515
00:53:02,053 --> 00:53:03,722
‎Bravo!

516
00:53:54,606 --> 00:53:55,774
‎Where did he disappear to?

517
00:53:55,857 --> 00:53:58,276
‎I don't know.
‎We can't get in touch with security.

518
00:54:01,947 --> 00:54:02,906
‎Excuse me.

519
00:54:02,989 --> 00:54:04,407
‎Is something going on?

520
00:54:04,908 --> 00:54:05,909
‎We're not sure yet,

521
00:54:05,992 --> 00:54:07,953
‎but the last finalist
‎still hasn't arrived.

522
00:54:13,833 --> 00:54:18,088
‎We regret to inform you
‎of some unfortunate news.

523
00:54:18,797 --> 00:54:21,091
‎The final contestant of the competition,

524
00:54:21,174 --> 00:54:24,636
‎Jeong-yo Choi, has gone missing.

525
00:54:25,512 --> 00:54:29,683
‎Therefore, today's final performance
‎has been canceled.

526
00:54:30,558 --> 00:54:33,353
‎The decision regarding the award ceremony

527
00:54:33,436 --> 00:54:37,816
‎will be decided as soon as the situation
‎has been assessed.

528
00:54:38,733 --> 00:54:39,567
‎Thank you.

529
00:54:46,658 --> 00:54:48,159
‎What do you mean Jeong-yo is missing?

530
00:54:48,243 --> 00:54:50,370
‎We don't know anything yet.

531
00:54:50,453 --> 00:54:52,831
‎We reported the situation to the police.

532
00:54:52,914 --> 00:54:55,166
‎But for the time being,

533
00:54:55,250 --> 00:54:57,085
‎please return to your accommodations

534
00:54:57,168 --> 00:54:59,963
‎and then we'll contact you individually.

535
00:55:23,695 --> 00:55:25,864
‎-Where have you been?
‎-You scared me!

536
00:55:45,884 --> 00:55:48,470
‎Why won't you even tell us
‎what you've found so far?

537
00:55:49,137 --> 00:55:50,346
‎Was he kidnapped?

538
00:55:50,430 --> 00:55:51,681
‎Was it an accident?

539
00:55:51,765 --> 00:55:54,184
‎Have you identified the driver
‎and the guard yet?

540
00:55:54,267 --> 00:55:55,101
‎Okay.

541
00:55:55,185 --> 00:55:57,270
‎There's nothing we can share at this time.

542
00:55:57,353 --> 00:56:01,066
‎What do you mean you can't tell me?
‎I'm his guardian!

543
00:56:01,149 --> 00:56:01,983
‎Stop, Hyun-jeong.

544
00:56:02,067 --> 00:56:04,194
‎These people don't know anything yet.

545
00:56:04,277 --> 00:56:06,988
‎How could something like this happen?

546
00:56:07,655 --> 00:56:08,823
‎What's going on?

547
00:56:09,407 --> 00:56:11,326
‎Is it true Jeong-yo has gone missing?

548
00:56:12,202 --> 00:56:13,620
‎Police are currently investigating

549
00:56:13,703 --> 00:56:16,247
‎whether this disappearance is related
‎to the recent kidnapping attacks

550
00:56:16,331 --> 00:56:17,332
‎carried out by…

551
00:56:27,050 --> 00:56:28,176
‎Where's Jeong-yo?

552
00:56:28,802 --> 00:56:30,011
‎They haven't found him yet.

553
00:56:31,971 --> 00:56:34,766
‎They haven't even located the car
‎he was in.

554
00:56:34,849 --> 00:56:35,934
‎We'll have to wait longer

555
00:56:37,310 --> 00:56:38,853
‎for the police investigation.

556
00:56:44,776 --> 00:56:46,528
‎Pi-o, are you okay?

557
00:56:50,698 --> 00:56:52,158
‎Don't worry too much.

558
00:56:54,285 --> 00:56:55,537
‎He'll be okay.

559
00:56:56,204 --> 00:56:57,997
‎They'll find him soon.

560
00:56:59,541 --> 00:57:01,000
‎I'm sure there was just a mix-up.

561
00:57:02,460 --> 00:57:06,131
‎So don't worry too much.

562
00:57:08,800 --> 00:57:09,634
‎Mom.

563
00:57:10,844 --> 00:57:11,761
‎Mom.

564
00:57:12,971 --> 00:57:14,139
‎Mom, did you…

565
00:57:48,715 --> 00:57:53,511
‎The winner of the Prague Harmonie
‎International Competition is

566
00:57:53,595 --> 00:57:55,930
‎Mr. Pi-o Kang.

567
00:58:50,735 --> 00:58:55,448
‎2026

568
00:58:59,369 --> 00:59:01,579
‎You look tired from the long trip.

569
00:59:01,663 --> 00:59:02,747
‎I'm fine.

570
00:59:02,830 --> 00:59:04,666
‎Did you secure the practice room?

571
00:59:05,416 --> 00:59:06,918
‎It was too late to find one,

572
00:59:07,001 --> 00:59:09,879
‎so we arranged a bar
‎across from the hotel.

573
00:59:09,963 --> 00:59:12,048
‎So you can use it after it closes.

574
00:59:12,882 --> 00:59:14,092
‎Will that be all right?

575
00:59:14,676 --> 00:59:15,969
‎That should be okay for now.

576
01:00:42,555 --> 01:00:44,474
‎I'VE MEMORIZED EVERYTHING.
‎TAKE IT IF YOU NEED IT!

577
01:01:04,577 --> 01:01:06,704
‎FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

578
01:01:06,788 --> 01:01:09,040
‎About that Choi Jeong-yo rumor…

579
01:01:09,123 --> 01:01:10,958
‎People say you were behind it.

580
01:01:11,042 --> 01:01:13,086
‎It's because of you.

581
01:01:13,169 --> 01:01:16,589
‎I found someone in Romania
‎who said they saw Mr. Choi.

582
01:01:16,673 --> 01:01:17,799
‎It was this man.

583
01:01:17,882 --> 01:01:19,509
‎I'd like to ask him myself.

584
01:01:19,592 --> 01:01:21,844
‎What did you do to Jeong-yo?

585
01:01:22,345 --> 01:01:23,513
‎What's in it for me?

586
01:01:24,597 --> 01:01:25,431
‎Tell me now!

587
01:01:26,015 --> 01:01:27,183
‎Do you even know how special he was?

588
01:01:27,684 --> 01:01:29,310
‎What exactly are you trying to confirm?

589
01:01:30,103 --> 01:01:31,688
‎Proof that Mr. Choi is alive?

590
01:01:32,355 --> 01:01:33,606
‎Or proof of his death?

591
01:01:35,233 --> 01:01:40,238
‎Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim
